+<cx "consonants, pronunciation of (quick-tour version)">  XE "consonants: =
pronunciation of, quick-tour version"   Twelve consonants in Lojban are pro=
nounced more or less as their counterparts are in English: =93b=94, =93d=94=
, =93f=94, =93k=94, =93l=94, =93m=94, =93n=94, =93p=94, =93r=94, =93t=94, =
=93v=94 and =93z=94. The letter =93c=94, on the other hand is pronounced as=
 the =93sh=94 in =93hush=94, while =93j=94 is its voiced counterpart, the s=
ound of the =93s=94 in =93pleasure=94. =93g=94 is always pronounced as it i=
s in =93gift=94, never as in =93giant=94. =93s=94 is as in =93sell=94, neve=
r as in =93rose=94. The sound of =93x=94 is not found in English in normal =
words. It is found as =93ch=94 in Scottish =93loch=94, as =93j=94 in Spanis=
h =93junta=94, and as =93ch=94 in German =93Bach=94; it also appears in the=
