+</dl><a name=3Ds10><h3>Considerations for making lujvo</h3>
+<p>
+Given a tanru which expresses an idea to be used frequently, it can be tur=
ned into a lujvo by following the lujvo-making algorithm which is given in =
<a href=3D#s11>Section 11</a>.
+<p>
+In building a lujvo, the first step is to replace each gismu with a rafsi =
that uniquely represents that gismu. These rafsi are then attached together=
 by fixed rules that allow the resulting compound to be recognized as a sin=
gle word and to be analyzed in only one way.
+<p>
+There are three other complications; only one is serious.
+<p>
+<cx "rafsi, multiple for each gismu">  XE "rafsi: multiple for each gismu"=
