+<pre><a name=3De14d6>14.6)	=93lanme=94:  l1 is a sheep of breed l2 belongi=
ng to flock l3
+	=93gerku=94:  g1 is a dog of breed g2
+	=93jitro=94:  j1 controls j2 in activity j3
+</pre><p>Note that this lujvo is symmetrical between =93lantro=94 (sheep-c=
ontroller) and =93gerku=94, but =93lantro=94 is itself a asymmetrical lujvo=
. The l2 place, the breed of sheep, is removed as dependent on l1. However,=
 the lujvo =93lange'u=94 is both shorter than =93terlantroge'u=94 and suffi=
ciently clear to warrant its use: its place structure, however, should be t=
he same as that of the longer lujvo, for which =93lange'u=94 can be underst=
ood as an abbreviation.
+<p>
+<ex "beckon">  XE "beckon: example=93  <cx "lujvo place order, elliptical =
lujvo">  XE "lujvo place order: elliptical lujvo"   Another example is =93x=
anmi'e=94, =93to command by hand, to beckon=94. The component place structu=
res are:
