+<a name=3Ds9><h3>The uses of indicators</h3>
+<p>
+<cx "attitudinals, grammar of placement in bridi">  XE "attitudinals: gram=
mar of placement in bridi"   <cx "attitudinals, external grammar">  XE "att=
itudinals: external grammar"   <lx "si">  XE "si"   <lx "sa">  XE "sa"   <l=
x "su">  XE "su"   The behavior of indicators in the =93outside grammar=94 =
is nearly as simple as their internal structure. Indicator groupings are id=
entified immediately after the metalinguistic erasers =93si=94, =93sa=94, a=
