+<p>
+<cx "subscripting, and pro-sumti">  XE =93subscripts: and pro-sumti"   <cx=
 "da-series, after third">  XE "da-series: after third"   <cx "ko'a-series,=
 after tenth">  XE "ko'a-series: after tenth"   Lojban provides two groups =
of pro-sumti, both belonging to selma'o KOhA. The ko'a-series cmavo are use=
d to refer to explicitly specified sumti to which they have been bound usin=
g =93goi=94. The da-series, on the other hand, are existentially or univers=
ally quantified variables. (These concepts are explained more fully in <a h=
ref=3Dchap16.html>Chapter 16</a>.)  There are ten ko'a-series cmavo and 3 d=
a-series cmavo available.
+<p>
+<lx "DA">  XE "DA selma=92o"   <lx "da">  XE "da"   If more are required, =
any cmavo of the ko'a-series or the da-series can be subscripted:
+<p>
+<pre><a name=3De6d7>6.7)	daxivo
