+<p>
+<pre><a name=3De13d9>13.9)	mi viska le blanu zdan. sa le xekri zdani
+	I see the blue hou=A0<dots>=85</dots>the black house.
+</pre><p>In <a href=3D#e13d9>Example 13.9</a>, =93le blanu zdan.=94 is ung=
rammatical, but clearly reflects the speaker's original intention to say =
=93le blanu zdani=94. However, the =93zdani=94 was cut off before the end a=
nd changed into a name. The entire ungrammatical =93le=94 construct is eras=
ed and replaced by =93le xekri zdani=94.
+
+<p>
+Note: The current machine parser does not implement =93sa=94 erasure. Gett=
ing =93sa=94 right is even more difficult (for a computer) than getting =93=
