+<p>
+The YACC grammar included herein is written to make YACC generation of a s=
tep 6 parser easy regardless of whether a. or b. is used. The strings of to=
kens to be labelled with lexer tokens are found in rule terminals labelled =
with numbers between 900 and 1099. These rules are defined with the lexer t=
okens inserted, with the result that it can be verified that the language i=
s LALR1 under option b. after steps 1 through 4 have been performed. Altern=
atively, if option a. is to be used, these rules are commented out, and the=
 rule terminals labelled from 800 to 900 refer to the lexer tokens without =
the strings of defining tokens. Two sets of lexer tokens are defined in the=
